                <pb facs="1118" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1008"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.156/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-09T16:00:00+08:00">November 9, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 9—6:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>895. Legation’s 899 [<hi rendition="#italic">869</hi>], November 4, 11
                        a.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d935-f1"/> Regarding foreshore regulations,
                    Japanese Legation now informs me Japanese Government not in a position to accept
                    revised regulations.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
